                        "source_sense_id": "c3a6db7d-d8c5-3c28-8db1-a5cbd76fcc91",
                        "source_sense_description": "das Alles-Wissen, das Wissen von Allem",
                        "target_lang_word": "omniscience",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "omniscience",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "28b87281-18bc-32d1-a49d-4d6d1f764f9a",
                                        "entry_id": "0e17e139-cecb-363e-a9e2-5f484d5dad3f",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "The capacity to know everything."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "bf895b74-43ad-46ae-b257-1779815b7ea9",
                                                "sense_id": "28b87281-18bc-32d1-a49d-4d6d1f764f9a",
                                                "text": "Near-synonyms: all-seeingness, omnividence"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "04842458-1d4b-4367-8dc1-a5cfb68cabe1",
                                                "sense_id": "28b87281-18bc-32d1-a49d-4d6d1f764f9a",
                                                "text": "Many people believe in God's omniscience."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "b349f669-54e0-450f-a6e6-09f469fe1306",
                                                "sense_id": "28b87281-18bc-32d1-a49d-4d6d1f764f9a",
                                                "text": "If, a few pages back, the present writer claimed the privilege of peeping into Miss Amelia Sedley's bedroom, and understanding with the omniscience the novelist all the gentle pains and passions which were tossing upon that innocent pillow, why should he not declare himself to be Rebecca's confidante too, master of her secrets, and seal-keeper of that young woman's conscience?"
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "895420eb-a028-4e9c-8736-100d7a5403d1",
                        "source_entry_id": "94ecaf1a-39e3-3982-95e3-e44f4d6ccfc0",
                        "source_sense_id": "c3a6db7d-d8c5-3c28-8db1-a5cbd76fcc91",
                        "source_sense_description": "das Alles-Wissen, das Wissen von Allem",
                        "target_lang_word": "omniscience",
                        "target_lang_code": "fr",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "omniscience",
                                "target_lang_code": "fr",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "87e8d83e-707e-3df8-9299-a8099b4c326a",
                                        "entry_id": "07ef1f7a-e2d3-3cf3-9972-8fe204d0d929",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Science de toute chose."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "note": "S’employait surtout, en termes de théologie, en parlant de Dieu. On l'emploie aussi dans un sens ironique pour se moquer des prétentieux, cuistres, etc",
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "054ab2a4-c16c-4c1a-8828-76e1baf4c991",
                                                "sense_id": "87e8d83e-707e-3df8-9299-a8099b4c326a",
                                                "text": "Ce pamphlet contre l’homme que Diderot n’osa pas publier, le Neveu de Rameau ; ce livre, débraillé tout exprès pour montrer des plaies, est seul comparable à ce pamphlet dit sans aucune arrière-pensée, où le mot ne respecta même point ce que le penseur discute encore, où l’on ne construisit qu’avec des ruines, où l’on nia tout, où l’on n’admira que ce que le scepticisme adopte : l’omnipotence, l’omniscience, l’omniconvenance de l’argent."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
